--
N5008 [expr.new]/24, [dcl.init.general]/16.5 (P0960, C++20): `new
int[3](1, 2)' initializes the elements from the parenthesized
expression-list as from a braced list (narrowing conversions aside): 1,
2, 0.  The front end reported it as unsupported (bin53 crashed); it now
takes the path of `new T[n]{...}'
(cpp11_array_new_value_and_list_initialization), and before C++20
reports that C++20 is required.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
